{"permission":"allow","user_message":"[persistent-cd] a persistent top-level directory change in the primary firstmate checkout already ran, so the shell is now outside the firstmate home and a later firstmate-owned command runs inside that directory. Run cd back to the firstmate home before any firstmate-owned command. Next time reach the target without moving the shell - use git -C <dir> or an absolute path on the command itself - or scope the cd to a subshell like (cd <dir> && ...)."}
